{
  "id": "26826_kaishisuru",
  "headword": "{開始|かいし}する",
  "reading": "かいしする",
  "romaji": "kaishisuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to start; to commence; to begin",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to start; to commence; to begin",
      "explanation": "To initiate or set something in motion, often used for formal or planned activities such as operations, services, projects, or events. More formal than {始|はじ}める."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "26826_kaishisuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{営業|えいぎょう}を{開始|かいし}する。",
      "english": "To commence business operations.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26826_kaishisuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{午前|ごぜん}{九時|くじ}に{会議|かいぎ}を{開始|かいし}します。",
      "english": "The meeting will begin at nine in the morning.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26826_kaishisuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{新|あたら}しいサービスの{提供|ていきょう}を{来月|らいげつ}から{開始|かいし}する{予定|よてい}です。",
      "english": "We plan to start offering the new service from next month.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26826_kaishisuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{工事|こうじ}が{予定|よてい}どおり{開始|かいし}された。",
      "english": "The construction commenced as scheduled.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal verb for starting or commencing an activity. While {始|はじ}める is used for everyday actions, {開始|かいし}する implies a deliberate, planned beginning and is common in business, official announcements, and written language.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {営業|えいぎょう}{開始|かいし}: start of business\n- {販売|はんばい}{開始|かいし}: start of sales\n- {運用|うんよう}{開始|かいし}: start of operation\n- サービス{開始|かいし}: service launch\n- {工事|こうじ}{開始|かいし}: start of construction\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {始|はじ}める: to begin — general-purpose, used for both casual and formal starting\n- {着手|ちゃくしゅ}する: to embark on — emphasizes taking the first step in a large project\n- スタートする: to start — casual, often used for races or new ventures",
